        "title": "Culture difference and Beauty of Tradition in Pashupatinath temple ",
        "text": "Travel can make mind outstretched. The oldest and holiest Hindu shrine in Nepal \"The Pashupatinath Temple\" located on the bank of Bagmati river is a world heritage site enlisted by UNESCO.The water flowing along the temple of Bagmati River is considered as holy and eventually flows into Ganga.\n      Only Hindu and Buddhist are allowed in a core of temple. Although it was a heartbreaking fact, the beauty of temple premises made to overthink what the beauty of core might be. I witnessed a funeral ritual  according to Hindu tradition: the fire, smoke; sadness and cryness of relatives of the deceased made be realise the pain when u loose your beloved one. It was a learning of a cultural difference and a beauty of tradition.",
